cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Joyglide
message: >-
  If you use this software or reference its protocol-research
  findings, please cite as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Thomaz
    family-names: Doronides
    email: tdoronides@gmail.com
    alias: opsthomaz
repository-code: 'https://github.com/opsthomaz/joyglide'
url: 'https://github.com/opsthomaz/joyglide'
abstract: >-
  Cross-platform desktop application that pairs a Nintendo Switch 2
  Joy-Con over Bluetooth Low Energy and uses its optical sensor as a
  native macOS / Windows mouse. The project also contributes
  hardware-verified corrections to the open Joy-Con 2 BLE protocol
  catalog — including the IMU timestamp scale (1 MHz, not 50 kHz),
  the battery-current scale (raw / 100 = mA), the feature-mask 0xFF
  requirement, and the write-command length-byte semantics. All
  protocol claims are tier-rated (S = hardware-verified, A = methodical
  reverse-engineering, B = official platform docs, etc.) and cross-
  checked against working third-party drivers in research/.
keywords:
  - joy-con
  - joycon
  - nintendo-switch-2
  - bluetooth-low-energy
  - ble
  - reverse-engineering
  - input-device
  - mouse
  - macos
  - windows
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.3
date-released: '2026-08-29'
